caption.en:
Professionals can have the EB2-NIW visa as a gateway to continue their career in the United States, based on exceptional ability. To do this, it is necessary to provide a series of evidence that demonstrates knowledge or long experience in a specific field.
The exceptional ability criterion has 6 requirements, of which at least 3 must be met:
- Official academic records obtained from accredited educational institutions. The academic record must be directly related to the applicant's area of ​​work;
- Proven experience of at least 10 years full-time in the occupation;
- Present the license or certification to exercise the profession or occupation;
- Prove above-average remuneration, compared to other professionals in the area, due to their skill, knowledge or qualification;
- Evidence of membership in professional associations related to your area of ​​activity;
- Demonstrate recognition for achievements and significant contributions to your industry or field.
It is important to remember that you must provide at least three of the pieces of evidence mentioned above, but you can also present other types of evidence to strengthen your case.
