caption.en:
Yes, Brazilian law protects passengers much more than other countries. It is important to know that according to Brazilian law, passengers have some specific rights. If the flight is canceled or delayed for more than 1 hour, the airline is obliged to provide assistance, no matter what the cause. Delay of more than 1 hour: right to communication (telephone, internet and others);
Delay of more than 2 hours: right to food; Delay of more than 4 hours: right to accommodation and transportation (if the passenger is not in the region where they live) or just transportation (if the airport is in the region where they live). Optionally, you can choose to receive a full refund or the same service on another type of transport.
Attention: PCD passengers and their companions will always have the right to accommodation. These rules apply to both domestic flights and flights originating in other countries to Brazil.
Did the company fail to comply with this? Seek to formalize a complaint to Anac and Procon. If the delay or cancellation caused any loss or damage, you may be entitled to a refund and compensation. Bus passengers also have rights. Link to find out more in Bio.
